{"name":"Tapeworm / sanitized parasite diet","deep":true,"image":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Desiccated_tapeworm_proglottids.jpg/960px-Desiccated_tapeworm_proglottids.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","credit":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Desiccated_tapeworm_proglottids.jpg","caption":"Desiccated tapeworm proglottids","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},"mentions":0,"casual":{"lead":["The tapeworm diet is a fringe idea of deliberately ingesting a tapeworm, or a pill said to contain one, to lose weight quickly and get thinner.","The idea is that a parasite absorbs part of the host's nutrient intake, so fewer calories are taken in. No studies were found testing it as a weight-loss method, and it is not an accepted medical treatment."],"sections":[{"h":"How people use it","paras":["It circulates as a historical and online diet notion, usually described through so-called sanitized parasite pills. Because it is not a recognised treatment, there is no established routine or timeline."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Risks & side effects","paras":["Infection with the pork tapeworm Taenia solium can cause cysticercosis, including cysts in the brain, and the resulting neurocysticercosis is described as the leading cause of seizures worldwide; severe cases can cause death. Treatment also needs medical monitoring. Anyone with a suspected infection should see a clinician."],"subs":[]}]},"gallery":[{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Desiccated_tapeworm_proglottids.jpg/960px-Desiccated_tapeworm_proglottids.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","full":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a7/Desiccated_tapeworm_proglottids.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","title":"Desiccated tapeworm proglottids","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","creator":"KDS444","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Desiccated_tapeworm_proglottids.jpg","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Egg_of_tapeworm_in_feces_microscopy.jpg/960px-Egg_of_tapeworm_in_feces_microscopy.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","full":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1f/Egg_of_tapeworm_in_feces_microscopy.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","title":"Egg of tapeworm in feces microscopy","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","creator":"Ajay Kumar Chaurasiya","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Egg_of_tapeworm_in_feces_microscopy.jpg","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Tapeworm_Taemia_pisiformis_Cysticercus_E.jpg/960px-Tapeworm_Taemia_pisiformis_Cysticercus_E.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","full":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/48/Tapeworm_Taemia_pisiformis_Cysticercus_E.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","title":"Tapeworm Taemia pisiformis Cysticercus E","license":"CC BY 4.0","creator":"Tgru001","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tapeworm_Taemia_pisiformis_Cysticercus_E.jpg","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Tapeworm_taenia_reproductive_segment.jpg/960px-Tapeworm_taenia_reproductive_segment.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","full":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/17/Tapeworm_taenia_reproductive_segment.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","title":"Tapeworm taenia reproductive segment","license":"CC BY 4.0","creator":"Tgru001","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tapeworm_taenia_reproductive_segment.jpg","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},{"url":"https://upload.w