ps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taenia_solium"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Fat loss","chain":["Parasite absorbs some nutrients","Claimed calorie loss","Rapid weight loss"],"effect":"claimed","text":"The tapeworm diet is a fringe idea in which people look to a parasite to reduce how many calories they absorb, aiming for rapid weight loss and a thinner body. It is not an accepted medical approach and has not been tested as a weight-loss method."},"wikipedia":null,"grokipedia":null,"lead":["The tapeworm or 'sanitized parasite' diet refers to the idea of deliberately ingesting a tapeworm, or a product claimed to contain one, in order to lose weight. It is discussed as a fringe weight-loss method, not an accepted medical treatment.","Tapeworm infection is a recognised medical condition. For the pork tapeworm Taenia solium, swallowing eggs can cause cysticercosis, in which cysts can form in the brain; the resulting neurocysticercosis is described as the leading cause of seizures worldwide [1]."],"infobox":[["Type","Fringe weight-loss practice"],["Mechanism claimed","Parasite absorbs nutrients"],["Medical status","Not an accepted treatment"]],"sections":[{"h":"Medical risks of tapeworm infection","paras":["Humans can acquire cysticercosis by swallowing T. solium eggs in contaminated food or water. Cysts in the brain can cause seizures, headaches, raised intracranial pressure, hydrocephalus, meningitis and, in severe cases, death [1].","Treatment itself needs careful monitoring because dying cysts can trigger inflammation, particularly in the brain [1]."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found testing deliberate tapeworm ingestion for weight loss or appearance."],"subs":[]}],"lore":null,"timeline":[],"refs":[{"title":"Taenia solium","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taenia_solium","source":"Wikipedia","year":2025,"type":"encyclopedia"}],"studies":[],"reddit":[],"forums":[]}